<header class="sp-head"><a class="sp-portrait" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi.jpg" alt="" width="104" height="104"></a><p class="featured-region">2 July 1849 · St Peter's Square, Rome</p><h1 class="sp-title">Garibaldi Leaves Rome</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>In the revolutions of 1848–49 the pope fled Rome and a republic was proclaimed in the city. A French army sent to restore papal rule besieged it for a month, and as the defences failed Giuseppe Garibaldi gathered his volunteers in St Peter's Square and invited those willing to fight on to follow him out of the city.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>I offer neither pay, nor quarters, nor food; I offer only hunger, thirst, forced marches, battles and death. Let him who loves his country with his heart, and not merely with his lips, follow me.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">As reported by his early biographers; the wording varies from one account to another.</p><div class="sp-full"><button type="button" class="sp-share" data-share-text="“I offer neither pay, nor quarters, nor food; I offer only hunger, thirst, forced marches, battles and death. Let him who loves his country with his heart, and not merely with his lips, follow me.” — Giuseppe Garibaldi, Garibaldi Leaves Rome" data-share-img="/images/og/speech-garibaldi-leaves-rome.jpg">Share this quote</button></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>Some four thousand men left with him, but they were hunted by French and Austrian troops, and his wife Anita died during the retreat. Garibaldi went into exile, returning to lead the Expedition of the Thousand in 1860, which won Sicily and Naples for the Kingdom of Italy proclaimed the following year.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-unification">Italian unification</a><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a></div></div></section>
